1
00:00:06,060 --> 00:00:07,220
I see you've been awake since early morning.

2
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:09,780
Aren't you going to get ready for work, bro?

3
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:13,280
I'm not going to the office these days.

4
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:15,420
Really? Then you should hurry up.

5
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:17,760
This shirt isn't ironed at all.

6
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:19,480
Yeah, I'm in a rush. It's fine.

7
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:22,520
Then why aren't you going to work, bro?

8
00:00:23,340 --> 00:00:25,340
They allow us to Work From Home.

9
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,560
In that case, I should do it too.

10
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:34,020
You have to ask for permission and get P'Best's approval first.

11
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:38,540
So how should I inform him?

12
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:42,080
Do I have to go sit and sip coffee with him?

13
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:47,540
I never used to see you drink coffee before though.

14
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:06,940
EP4 "Familiar"

15
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:15,180
P'Best.

16
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:16,660
P'Best, sir.

17
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:20,140
P'Tontae, bro.

18
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:23,480
Can I go help P'Dan with his work at his condo?

19
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:27,300
Well, he's alone, so I'm worried he might get tired.

20
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:29,520
Besides, my work is quite similar to his.

21
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:31,580
That's pretty strange.

22
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:32,740
Ask P'Best yourself then.

23
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:36,100
P'Best, Pond has something to ask you, sir.

24
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:37,300
Yes, what is it?

25
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:39,580
P'Best, sir.

26
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:42,980
May I have permission to work at the condo with...

27
00:02:42,980 --> 00:02:44,340
P'Dan, please?

28
00:02:44,340 --> 00:02:45,740
Work at the condo?

29
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:48,660
Why do you need to go work at the condo?

30
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:51,700
Well, P'Dan is there all by himself.

31
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:53,060
Why are you grabbing my shoulder?

32
00:02:53,060 --> 00:02:53,960
Come on...

33
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:55,620
I'm worried he'll get exhausted, and besides,

34
00:02:55,620 --> 00:02:57,780
he needs to train me on the job too.

35
00:02:59,780 --> 00:03:01,400
So I thought...

36
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:07,080
If you're going, then go quickly.

37
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:09,200
So it's a yes, right?

38
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:10,600
Yes. Go on.

39
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:13,040
Okay, bro. Thank you so much.

40
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:14,840
Thank you, P'Best.

41
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:20,340
You can hold my shoulder though.

42
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:23,660
Can I hold it with both hands?

43
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:31,120
Hey, Best.

44
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:32,420
Didn't you say you were gonna help me?

45
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:35,280
I helped you as much as I could, P'Dan.

46
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:37,740
Instead of blocking him, you sent him straight to me?

47
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:41,060
I tried to block him, but that was the best I could do.

48
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:42,340
Your boy is just relentless.

49
00:03:42,340 --> 00:03:44,800
Alright, remember this. When it's your turn,

50
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:45,780
I won't help you either.

51
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:48,820
P'Dan, bro.

52
00:03:48,820 --> 00:03:50,440
Food is ready.

53
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:51,800
Well, well.

54
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:54,160
Having someone cook for you at your room...

55
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:55,500
might actually be nice sometimes.

56
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,340
Maybe not for this guy though.

57
00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:12,460
I'm hungry, bro.

58
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:14,840
We're out of groceries too.

59
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:16,400
Are you hungry?

60
00:04:17,540 --> 00:04:18,580
I'm not hungry.

61
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:21,320
It's already 10 PM.

62
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,560
So what?

63
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:27,120
Well, I'm hungry.

64
00:04:30,620 --> 00:04:32,880
Did you hear me say I'm hungry?

65
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:40,340
That is sweet.

66
00:04:44,220 --> 00:04:45,260
But I'm still not full.

67
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:48,720
You can go by yourself.

68
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:53,440
Well, if you don't go out to eat with me...

69
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:55,980
then I'm gonna eat you.

70
00:04:58,340 --> 00:04:58,940
Huh!

71
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,580
Fine, let's go eat.

72
00:05:19,620 --> 00:05:21,040
Now I'm full and satisfied.

73
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:24,020
Got the ingredients for P'Som-O's birthday gift too,

74
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:25,340
all set.

75
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:27,160
Feelin' good now, P'Dan.

76
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:30,440
Honestly...

77
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:33,060
If I had gone to buy them myself,

78
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:34,620
I would've finished ages ago.

79
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:36,400
Hey, I came along to help carry them.

80
00:05:38,100 --> 00:05:39,780
So you wouldn't have to carry them alone.

81
00:05:40,100 --> 00:05:40,640
It's heavy.

82
00:05:41,780 --> 00:05:43,020
I could really have carried them myself.

83
00:05:43,020 --> 00:05:43,500
Hey...

84
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,220
It's fine.

85
00:05:46,080 --> 00:05:47,080
I want to carry them.

86
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,340
I just want you...

87
00:05:48,340 --> 00:05:50,300
to take it easy.

88
00:05:53,060 --> 00:05:54,480
Yeah, right. Let's go back to work.

89
00:05:55,740 --> 00:05:58,400
But I don't wanna go back yet, P'Dan.

90
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:01,460
There happens to be a late-night movie show.

91
00:06:02,020 --> 00:06:03,100
I wanna watch a movie.

92
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:06,040
Shall we go watch a movie together?

93
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:08,340
But we're almost at the condo.

94
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:10,560
We're almost at the cinema too.

95
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:12,160
They're in opposite directions.

96
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:14,300
The cinema is way over there.

97
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:15,600
Are you crazy?

98
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,760
Woah, the condo is way over there too.

99
00:06:17,760 --> 00:06:19,400
I wanna watch it. Let me go.

100
00:06:20,400 --> 00:06:21,280
No way.

101
00:06:21,280 --> 00:06:23,020
Come on, I really wanna see it.

102
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:25,060
It's fine, I'll help you work later.

103
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:26,420
Or do you prefer working alone?

104
00:06:26,420 --> 00:06:28,680
Let's go.

105
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:29,860
Come on, let's go.

106
00:06:31,400 --> 00:06:32,520
Huh?

107
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:34,300
Aren't those P'Tontae and P'Best?

108
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:37,720
Hey, let's go say hi to them.

109
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:38,540
Hey!

110
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:40,600
Why?

111
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:42,640
Well, if you're gonna say hi to them...

112
00:06:43,060 --> 00:06:44,400
you have to let go of my hand first.

113
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:47,560
Then I won't let go.

114
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:49,280
I won't go say hi anymore.

115
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:52,080
Let them have their time together, and we'll have ours.

116
00:06:53,380 --> 00:06:54,240
One-on-one.

117
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:55,020
Even Steven.

118
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:57,320
Just come watch the movie with me.

119
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:58,440
My treat today.

120
00:06:58,440 --> 00:06:59,440
You can let go of my hand now.

121
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:00,740
Yeah, let's go.

122
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:04,480
I really like this movie too.

123
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:05,460
Let go already.

124
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:06,580
Oh, it's fine.

125
00:07:06,580 --> 00:07:09,520
Man, your grip is tight.

126
00:07:26,460 --> 00:07:27,280
Oh, bro.

127
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:29,440
Just now...

128
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:31,140
I thought I saw...

129
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:32,320
Pond...

130
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,160
coming along with P'Dan.

131
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,400
Just now?

132
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:37,360
Yeah.

133
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:40,780
I think so too.

134
00:07:43,780 --> 00:07:44,780
Do you think...

135
00:07:44,780 --> 00:07:46,340
those two...

136
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:49,600
stand a chance?

137
00:07:50,940 --> 00:07:53,760
Hmm, do you know something about them?

138
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:57,200
I don't really know much, bro.

139
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:59,340
All I know is that Pond...

140
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:01,680
is currently pursuing P'Dan.

141
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:04,980
So do you think...

142
00:08:04,980 --> 00:08:07,380
Pond stands a chance, bro?

143
00:08:07,960 --> 00:08:09,140
Hmm...

144
00:08:09,140 --> 00:08:11,280
I'm not sure if Pond stands a chance either.

145
00:08:14,380 --> 00:08:17,180
If you don't know whether Pond stands a chance...

146
00:08:17,180 --> 00:08:18,820
then...

147
00:08:21,460 --> 00:08:22,680
do you think...

148
00:08:25,780 --> 00:08:27,840
I stand a chance with you, bro?

149
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:35,980
It's already dark outside.

150
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:38,800
The condo isn't far either.

151
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:42,700
If you want to stay over tonight...

152
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:43,820
you can.

153
00:08:47,760 --> 00:08:49,120
In that case...

154
00:08:53,820 --> 00:08:55,800
I'd better head off first, bro.

155
00:09:14,520 --> 00:09:15,360
*Sigh*...

156
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:17,520
Hey, Pond.

157
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:20,580
Yes, bro?

158
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:22,640
There's no progress on my end at all.

159
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:24,740
Nothing happened whatsoever.

160
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:26,760
Isn't it good that nothing happened?

161
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:28,580
Or did you actually want something to happen?

162
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:30,680
Well...

163
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:33,860
He isn't even taking me seriously.

164
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:36,020
So it's good that nothing happened.

165
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:39,660
But he already invited me to sleep over at his condo.

166
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:42,620
And what did he say?

167
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:43,900
He said...

168
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:46,480
it's getting late, why not sleep over, or something like that.

169
00:09:48,260 --> 00:09:50,400
Well, there you go. He was just being caring.

170
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:52,160
I think it means he has feelings for me.

171
00:09:52,160 --> 00:09:54,260
Because if he didn't care...

172
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,800
he wouldn't have invited me to stay over.

173
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:58,040
I don't think so.

174
00:09:58,040 --> 00:10:00,120
It's more like a coworker thing.

175
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:02,900
You sure know how to crush my dreams.

176
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:05,280
Look on the bright side.

177
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:06,120
If he didn't like me...

178
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:07,900
why would he invite me to his condo?

179
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:10,140
Even though P'Dan doesn't like me...

180
00:10:10,140 --> 00:10:11,980
he still went to watch a movie with me.

181
00:10:12,580 --> 00:10:13,680
P'Dan went to the movies with you?

182
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:14,620
Yeah.

183
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:15,280
And how did it go?

184
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:16,500
The lonely guy, right?

185
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:18,460
Man... he fell asleep 3 minutes in.

186
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Or maybe...

187
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:24,400
do we need to be more serious about this?

188
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:28,440
Exactly! I think it's time to take it seriously.

189
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:29,480
How serious?

190
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:30,900
What do you mean by serious?

191
00:10:31,220 --> 00:10:32,240
"Wrong only 8 times..."

192
00:10:32,240 --> 00:10:34,060
That's enough. You're not being serious.

193
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:36,200
Come on.

194
00:10:36,980 --> 00:10:38,320
Let's get more serious.

195
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:40,820
Both you and me, let's go.

196
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:42,200
I've already started.

197
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:44,200
I've been serious for a long time. It's just you!

198
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,500
Go, get going!

199
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:47,160
Aren't you going too, bro?

200
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:48,820
Just go.

201
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:50,860
Come on, bro, go!

202
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:53,400
Wait... why aren't you going?

203
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:56,880
See? You're not serious. No wonder Dan won't take you.

204
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:58,300
Ouch... Don't worry about P'Dan.

205
00:10:58,300 --> 00:10:59,980
I've got him completely under control.

206
00:10:59,980 --> 00:11:00,660
You're the one who can't handle it.

207
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:03,160
Go! The more you talk, the more you curse yourself.

208
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:14,080
Ordering the Teriyaki Chicken...

209
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:15,880
but not eating green onions?

210
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:18,580
Usually, the restaurant doesn't put them in for me.

211
00:11:18,580 --> 00:11:20,300
It was probably busy this time,

212
00:11:20,300 --> 00:11:21,960
so they forgot.

213
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:23,540
I just dislike green onions.

214
00:11:23,540 --> 00:11:24,900
The smell is too pungent.

215
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:28,480
Coming here so often...

216
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,460
I believe you really love this restaurant.

217
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:33,540
I love it very much.

218
00:11:38,540 --> 00:11:40,400
It's not just the restaurant that I like.

219
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:45,360
The Khua Kling is delicious, isn't it?

220
00:11:51,060 --> 00:11:52,520
I want to tell you...

221
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,240
I'm even more delicious than Khua Kling.

222
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:26,680
Do it properly.

223
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:33,460
Spread it evenly.

224
00:12:37,060 --> 00:12:38,560
You never used to wear glasses before.

225
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:41,500
Why are you wearing them nowadays?

226
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:44,820
Whether I wear them or not is my business, right?

227
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:46,680
These are my eyes, not yours.

228
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:48,820
What does it matter to you whether I wear them or not?

229
00:12:49,660 --> 00:12:51,340
You look cute with them on.

230
00:12:54,220 --> 00:12:55,180
Whoa.

231
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:59,620
Look at this. Spread it.

232
00:12:59,840 --> 00:13:01,300
This is the last piece already.

233
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:07,360
You've changed a lot, haven't you?

234
00:13:08,180 --> 00:13:09,460
Really?

235
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:14,160
Do you know...

236
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:16,220
In just a few years...

237
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:19,580
you've changed so much.

238
00:13:22,180 --> 00:13:23,800
Haven't you changed too?

239
00:13:27,620 --> 00:13:29,120
How could I change?

240
00:13:30,060 --> 00:13:31,400
When...

241
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:33,660
you left me behind in the exact same place.

242
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:44,060
The place where I stay...

243
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:48,240
is still completely filled with memories of you.

244
